<title>BELGIUM: Austria wins extra EU durum wheat aid.</title>
<headline>Austria wins extra EU durum wheat aid.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-06-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Austria won extra aid for durum wheat producers as part of the European Union's 1997/98 farm price package, Austrian diplomats said on Thursday.</p>
<p>Farmers in the Pannonia region, east of Vienna, who have traditionally grown durum wheat will be entitled to aid of 358.6 Ecus per hectare instead of 138.9 Ecus, under the 1997/98 EU farm price package agreed in Luxembourg on Wednesday.</p>
<p>But the durum wheat area eligible for the aid remains at 5,000 hectares.</p>
<p>--Brussels bureau +322 287 6830</p>
</text>
